# DSML — Design System Mali Rules for Cursor & AI Agents

You are assisting with development using DSML (Design System Mali). Always adhere to the following rules:

1. **Design Tokens & Colors:**
   - Use official Malian republican colors: Green (`var(--ml-color-green-500)`), Gold (`var(--ml-color-gold-400)`), Red (`var(--ml-color-red-600)`).
   - Use cultural palettes when appropriate: Bogolan (`var(--ml-color-bogolan-ocre)`), Indigo (`var(--ml-color-indigo-600)`), Fleuve Niger (`var(--ml-color-river-500)`).

2. **Typography & Styling:**
   - Title font: Archivo
   - Body font: Atkinson Hyperlegible
   - Avoid generic colors (plain blue, plain red). Always use DSML variables or Tailwind utility classes mapped to DSML tokens.

3. **Accessibility (a11y):**
   - Ensure all interactive elements have visible focus indicators (`focus:ring-2 focus:ring-[var(--ml-color-green-400)]`).
   - Include ARIA attributes (`aria-describedby`, `aria-label`, `role`) on form elements and banners.

4. **Code Quality:**
   - Favor HTML + Tailwind snippets over unnecessary JavaScript framework wrappers.
   - Keep comments in technical English when required, self-documenting code preferred.

5. **Git Flow & Commits:**
   - Follow Conventional Commits: `<type>(<scope>): <description>` (e.g. `feat(core): ...`, `fix(vue): ...`).
   - Use dedicated branch prefixes: `feat/<scope>-<name>`, `fix/<scope>-<name>`, `docs/<name>`.

